0 #edb/ref 17592186366228 13194139535786 true] [17592186366224 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366229 13194139535786 true] [17592186366224 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535786 true] [17592186366224 1041 "selection" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366224 1104 #edb/ref 17592186366229 13194139535786 true] [17592186366224 1110 #uuid "1a25362f-7a37-53ad-b176-ac4690cc5a2e" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366225 1034 "$P$ and $R$ only" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366225 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535786 true] [17592186366225 1111 #uuid "59a76543-a774-5b9b-b5f0-1e17e9393afe" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366226 1034 "$Q$ and $R$ only" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366226 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535786 true] [17592186366226 1111 #uuid "d27ab497-ceaf-5ef4-9a68-4412c3944c02" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366227 1034 "$R$ only" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366227 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535786 true] [17592186366227 1111 #uuid "b5cc5e49-d0e7-5fa2-9c23-7d0160ad40cd" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366228 1034 "$Q$ only" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366228 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535786 true] [17592186366228 1111 #uuid "87311d2b-b692-5387-8d7e-f90d38738534" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366229 1034 "$P$ and $Q$ only" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366229 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535786 true] [17592186366229 1111 #uuid "7763240f-e922-5814-83ba-21a7c4162901" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366230 1017 #edb/ref 17592186366231 13194139535786 true] [17592186366230 1089 "q-143687" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366230 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535786 true] [17592186366230 1100 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The sum of two $n\\times n$ diagonal matrices is always symmetric.\n- If $A$ is *any*  $n\\times n$  matrix, then $A-{A}^{T}$ is always symmetric.\n- The product of two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is always symmetric." 13194139535786 true] [17592186366230 1113 #uuid "966e8499-782e-5d3b-b3cd-5b0bce9e8db5" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366230 1145 "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for any diagonal matrices $A$ and $B,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A+B)^{T} & ={A}^{T}+{B}^{T} \\\\  & =A+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. As a counterexample, consider the matrix \n\n$\\,$ $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nHowever, $A-{A}^{T}$ is not symmetric:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-{A}^{T} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. As a counterexample, consider the symmetric matrices \n\n$\\,$ $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nHowever, their product is not symmetric:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366231 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366232 13194139535786 true] [17592186366231 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366233 13194139535786 true] [17592186366231 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366234 13194139535786 true] [17592186366231 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366235 13194139535786 true] [17592186366231 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366236 13194139535786 true] [17592186366231 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535786 true] [17592186366231 1041 "selection" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366231 1104 #edb/ref 17592186366233 13194139535786 true] [17592186366231 1110 #uuid "ff7e77df-ebf8-53c4-953e-4cbbdfd363b2" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366232 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366232 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535786 true] [17592186366232 1111 #uuid "cd0f9501-1f4e-5760-8e72-616db8a35e1a" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366233 1034 "I only" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366233 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535786 true] [17592186366233 1111 #uuid "797ef5c8-6ccd-5ad9-bde4-d0940899a6a2" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366234 1034 "III only" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366234 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535786 true] [17592186366234 1111 #uuid "c54b6bae-c139-5507-87e1-c3f8bc233780" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366235 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366235 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535786 true] [17592186366235 1111 #uuid "9b4b2678-5772-554a-8a50-567b0d5d5599" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366236 1034 "II only" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366236 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535786 true] [17592186366236 1111 #uuid "9ebc2625-8c3e-5089-ae2a-0b00470eb879" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366237 1017 #edb/ref 17592186366238 13194139535786 true] [17592186366237 1089 "q-143688" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366237 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535786 true] [17592186366237 1100 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $A$ is symmetric, then ${A}^{-1}$ is always symmetric (if it exists).\n- The sum of *any* two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is always symmetric.\n- If $A$ is *any*  $n\\times n$ matrix, then ${A}^{T}A$ is always symmetric." 13194139535786 true] [17592186366237 1113 #uuid "0b4af280-6359-53fe-9a66-22b4e15e0bb7" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366237 1145 "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for any non-singular symmetric matrix $A,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({A}^{-1})^{T} & =({A}^{T})^{-1} \\\\  & ={A}^{-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any two symmetric matrices $A$ and $B,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A+B)^{T} & ={A}^{T}+{B}^{T} \\\\  & =A+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any $m\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({A}^{T}A)^{T} & ={A}^{T}({A}^{T})^{T} \\\\  & ={A}^{T}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366238 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366239 13194139535786 true] [17592186366238 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366240 13194139535786 true] [17592186366238 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366241 13194139535786 true] [17592186366238 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366242 13194139535786 true] [17592186366238 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366243 13194139535786 true] [17592186366238 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535786 true] [17592186366238 1041 "selection" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366238 1104 #edb/ref 17592186366239 13194139535786 true] [17592186366238 1110 #uuid "1a0b28dc-2dd5-557a-9851-7bf252348c0e" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366239 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366239 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535786 true] [17592186366239 1111 #uuid "36ce0de3-76df-5deb-ace6-2afd08e69c95" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366240 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366240 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535786 true] [17592186366240 1111 #uuid "3609c658-ab43-51fe-a392-9a9e2248b8a2" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366241 1034 "I only" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366241 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535786 true] [17592186366241 1111 #uuid "b2170d32-3899-5ed0-b686-f326535768a7" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366242 1034 "III only" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366242 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535786 true] [17592186366242 1111 #uuid "f4a4c9f6-bc0c-542f-a9e7-88c82e1150db" 13194139535786 true] [17592186366243 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535786 true] [1759218636624